{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "id": "20260917-v3-stage-cp04a-p2-target-root",
  "title": "V3 stage-oriented refactor CP04a \u2014 P2 prerequisite: package/target root separation and domain authority registry",
  "goal": "Let every guard verdict-chain script read package code, configuration and generated projects from the package it runs from and target data only from an explicit target root, register the domain authorities detectors read with D18 trust roles, declare each gate's trust inputs and their sources, and prove that a package copy outside the repository reaches the same verdicts as the in-place run.",
  "acceptanceCriteria": [
    "Specialized, quality, historical integrity, CI contract and manifest scripts take the target from -TargetRoot or GUARD_TARGET_ROOT and package configuration from their own package, Invoke-V3 accepts -GenerationRoot, and in-place defaults and verdicts are unchanged.",
    "policy/authorities.json registers every domain authority read by package engine scripts with a default role and JSON Pointer roles validated by contracts/authorities.schema.json, and every pointer resolves in the target.",
    "Every stage gate declares trust contract inputs with base, head-candidate, derived-candidate or head-target sources, and the manifest check fails on an unregistered literal read, an undeclared or unread detector authority, a source that contradicts the role, or a projection consumed without its authority.",
    "Test-IFXTargetRootSeparation shows equal verdicts for Validate, Pre, HistoricalIntegrity, G03, G04, G05 and Plan04 between the in-place run and a package copy outside the repository against a target worktree without package code, its two negative controls fail, and it runs in v3-cross-platform on Linux and Windows.",
    "All existing guard tests pass, no protected path is moved or deleted, and the 13 required check names are unchanged."
  ],
